ath10k-ct: pci: run NAPI in a kthread

On ipq806x all PCIe MSIs are chained through one GIC interrupt that
is pinned to CPU0, so the RX/TX-completion work of the radios cannot
be moved by IRQ affinity and competes with NSS host traffic on CPU0.
Threaded NAPI lets the scheduler (or packet steering) put that work
on the other CPU. snoc already does the same.

--- a/ath10k-6.18/pci.c
+++ b/ath10k-6.18/pci.c
@@ -3568,6 +3568,7 @@ static void ath10k_pci_free_irq(struct a
 void ath10k_pci_init_napi(struct ath10k *ar)
 {
 	netif_napi_add(ar->napi_dev, &ar->napi, ath10k_pci_napi_poll);
+	dev_set_threaded(ar->napi_dev, true);
 }

 static int ath10k_pci_init_irq(struct ath10k *ar)
